{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.strict_increase","record":{"id":"support.strict_increase","kind":"claim","label":"Full relative support forces strict increase","status":"unverified","source_id":"support_tex_variation","locator":"variation.tex:247–249; Support/Closure.lean:47–67","statement":"For gamma in U and a Stieltjes measure mu with full relative support [0,1), every 0<=a<b<1 has mu((a,b))>0. Hence gamma(b)-gamma(a)=mu((a,b])>0. In particular every admissible minimizer is strictly increasing once support.full_relative_support has been applied.","assumption_ids":[],"evidence_ids":["support_source_bindings_20261024","support_graph_semantic_review_pending"],"citation_ids":["support_closure_source","support_closure_lean_source"],"boundary":"Curated source-level mathematical statement, not an elaborated Lean extraction or independently accepted proof. Its displayed local hypotheses are quantified guards; a hypothetical plateau is not an added premise of the full-support theorem. No differentiability or density is inferred from strict increase or full support. The implication only needs the cumulative convention and positive mass in every nonempty open interval."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.strict_increase","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/69473417dc487cafa5e2e39b3168d2c4a8bffdad2e91b6e486de48f122dda071","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]},{"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/77f0cf29ab577b42d8caa5b2831ebfb1ca170d4b13c1ef6897cadc8e93c2a834","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]},{"stage":"expository","subgraph_ref":"sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4